# CODEOWNERS — task S1-C07.
#
# Listed owners are requested for review automatically on any PR touching their
# paths, which is how the plan's "Sagnik reviews every backend PR" (S1-C01)
# happens without anyone remembering to add him.
#
# EVERY LINE IS COMMENTED OUT until the real GitHub usernames are filled in.
# GitHub silently ignores a CODEOWNERS entry naming a user who does not exist or
# lacks write access — you get no review request and no error, which is worse
# than having no file. Get each person's handle from their profile URL
# (github.com/<handle>), replace the placeholders, and uncomment.
#
# Also required: the owners must have write access to the repo, and for the rule
# to be enforced rather than advisory, enable "Require review from Code Owners"
# in the branch-protection settings for main.

# Fallback owner for anything not matched below.
# *                       @pankuzj

